public with sharing class AccountScoringJob implements Queueable {

    private static final Integer BATCH_SIZE = 200;
    private static final Decimal HOT_THRESHOLD = 1000000;
    private static final Decimal WARM_THRESHOLD = 100000;

    private final List<Id> accountIds;

    public AccountScoringJob(List<Id> accountIds) {
        this.accountIds = accountIds == null ? new List<Id>() : accountIds;
    }

    public static Id start(List<Id> accountIds) {
        if (accountIds == null || accountIds.isEmpty()) {
            return null;
        }
        Integer chunks = (Integer) Math.ceil(accountIds.size() / (Decimal) BATCH_SIZE);
        // The stack depth can only be set on the initial enqueue (outside a queueable);
        // chained jobs inherit it.
        AsyncOptions options = new AsyncOptions();
        options.MaximumQueueableStackDepth = chunks;
        return System.enqueueJob(new AccountScoringJob(accountIds), options);
    }

    public void execute(QueueableContext context) {
        if (accountIds.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        Integer batchEnd = Math.min(BATCH_SIZE, accountIds.size());
        Set<Id> batchIds = new Set<Id>();
        for (Integer i = 0; i < batchEnd; i++) {
            batchIds.add(accountIds[i]);
        }

        List<Account> toUpdate = new List<Account>();
        for (Account a : [SELECT Id, AnnualRevenue, Rating FROM Account WHERE Id IN :batchIds]) {
            a.Rating = rate(a.AnnualRevenue);
            toUpdate.add(a);
        }
        if (!toUpdate.isEmpty()) {
            update toUpdate;
        }

        if (accountIds.size() > batchEnd) {
            List<Id> remaining = new List<Id>();
            for (Integer i = batchEnd; i < accountIds.size(); i++) {
                remaining.add(accountIds[i]);
            }
            System.enqueueJob(new AccountScoringJob(remaining));
        }
    }

    private static String rate(Decimal revenue) {
        if (revenue != null && revenue >= HOT_THRESHOLD) {
            return 'Hot';
        }
        if (revenue != null && revenue >= WARM_THRESHOLD) {
            return 'Warm';
        }
        return 'Cold';
    }
}
```

I changed one thing: chained jobs now call plain `System.enqueueJob(job)` and no longer pass `AsyncOptions`. Salesforce only lets `MaximumQueueableStackDepth` be set on the initial enqueue from outside a queueable, and that is what caused the `AsyncException`. `start` still sets the depth to ⌈Ids ÷ 200⌉, and I expect the chained jobs to inherit it. I have not re-run the tests.

The error says only top-level classes can implement `Database.Batchable`, so the inner batch class had to go. `LogPurgeJob` now implements both `Schedulable` and `Database.Batchable<SObject>` itself. The scheduled `execute` hands the same class to `Database.executeBatch`, so the purge can handle more than 10,000 rows. I haven't deployed or run this against the tests.

