Rule 1 was never running on update. fflib calls only `onValidate(Map<Id,SObject>)` on update, not `onValidate()`, so the update paths had no negative-amount check. I haven't re-run the tests, and the insert failure isn't explained by this cause, so I can't confirm the fix covers it.

The corrected class puts both rules in the update hook. It also adds at most one error per record, so a record that breaks both rules is not counted twice in `Errors`.

