The previous version failed because `Account.Name` is required at the database level, so an account can't be inserted without a name. NPSP only fills the name in for accounts it creates itself.

This version lets NPSP create the household. It inserts the contacts with no `AccountId`, so NPSP creates a Household Account (`HH_Account` record type) for each one. It then re-parents everyone onto the first contact's household and removes the leftover households. I haven't run it against the test class.

